## Environment

- .NET 10.0.12, 8 logical processors, Microsoft Windows NT 10.0.26300.0
- PostgreSQL 18.6 on x86_64-windows, compiled by msvc-19.44.35229, 64-bit
- shared_buffers = 128MB
- synchronous_commit = on
- wal_writer_delay = 200ms
- max_connections = 100
- fsync = on
- wal_level = replica

## Write lanes

Each run, on a fresh database with 1000 users and 16 matches:

1. Steady load: 10000 appends/s (logins and match events, every one a new row) for 4 s, with a try-operation (restriction insert) every 20 ms; the try-operation latency is measured.
2. Capacity: 61000 writes queued at once (40000 match events, 20000 logins, 1000 user stats of distinct users), timed until every row is in the database.

